> system:
  You are a concise travel planner.
  You must call lookup_city_facts before producing the recommendation.
  Ground every returned field in the tool result.

@lookup_city_facts(city: str) -> str:
  ###
  Return a compact fact record for a known city.

  Args:
      city: City name to look up.
  ###
  = ```
  facts = {
      "Kyoto": "city=Kyoto; country=Japan; timezone=Asia/Tokyo; landmark=Fushimi Inari; note=Best for temples and quiet walking routes.",
      "Lisbon": "city=Lisbon; country=Portugal; timezone=Europe/Lisbon; landmark=Belem Tower; note=Best for hills, trams, and Atlantic food.",
      "Reykjavik": "city=Reykjavik; country=Iceland; timezone=Atlantic/Reykjavik; landmark=Hallgrimskirkja; note=Best for northern lights day trips.",
  }
  return facts.get(city, f"city={city}; country=Unknown; timezone=Unknown; landmark=Unknown; note=No curated note.")
  ```

> use: lookup_city_facts

>> Pick one city from Kyoto, Lisbon, or Reykjavik for a two-day culture trip. Use lookup_city_facts for the chosen city, then return [recommendation: Annotated[CityRecommendation, "Tool-grounded city recommendation"]].

